f fully corrected with hearing aids. Speaking in a high-pitched voice is counterproductive because high frequencies are lost first; instead, speak in a clear, deep, low-pitched voice facing the patient. (Ref: Hazzard''s Ch. 12, Ch. 46; Livingston et al., Lancet 2020)'),
