 to serious risks (volume depletion, hypokalemia, nocturnal polyuria leading to falls, orthostatic hypotension). The correct management is to recognize the cascade, **discontinue the loop diuretic**, and address the primary drug (stop/reduce amlodipine and substitute it with an ACE inhibitor or ARB, which do not cause significant edema). (Ref: Rochon & Gurwitz, BMJ 1997; Hazzard''s Ch. 30)'),
